# Visualize MABe Mouse Triplets

This Runme notebook uses the data loader and visualization helpers to inspect raw sequences and future model rollouts.

## Load One Window

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
from pathlib import Path
import sys

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src/data").exists())
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from data import MabeDataset, MabeWindowDataset, WindowSpec, fill_missing_keypoints

dataset = MabeDataset.from_file(repo_root / "data/mabe/raw/mouse_triplet_train.npy")
sequence = dataset.sequences[dataset.sequence_ids[0]]

clean_keypoints = fill_missing_keypoints(sequence.keypoints)
print("sequence:", sequence.sequence_id)
print("keypoints:", clean_keypoints.shape)
print("annotations:", sequence.annotations.shape)

windows = MabeWindowDataset(
    [sequence],
    spec=WindowSpec(length=20, observation_length=8, prediction_length=12, stride=20),
    max_windows=1,
)
window = windows.first()
print("window:", window.keypoints.shape)
```

## Animate a Raw Sequence Segment

In notebook environments, display the returned animation object. In terminal runs, use the save step below.

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
from pathlib import Path
import sys

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src/data").exists())
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from data import MabeDataset, fill_missing_keypoints
from matplotlib import rc

from data.visualization import animate_pose_sequence

dataset = MabeDataset.from_file(repo_root / "data/mabe/raw/mouse_triplet_train.npy")
sequence = dataset.sequences[dataset.sequence_ids[0]]
clean_keypoints = fill_missing_keypoints(sequence.keypoints)
rc("animation", html="jshtml")

animation_obj = animate_pose_sequence(
    clean_keypoints,
    sequence_id=sequence.sequence_id,
    start_frame=0,
    stop_frame=240,
    step=6,
    interval_ms=80,
)

animation_obj
```

## Save a Raw Sequence Animation

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
SEQ_ID = 2

from pathlib import Path
import sys

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src/data").exists())
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from data import MabeDataset, fill_missing_keypoints
from data.visualization import animate_pose_sequence
from data.visualization import save_animation

dataset = MabeDataset.from_file(repo_root / "data/mabe/raw/mouse_triplet_train.npy")
sequence = dataset.sequences[dataset.sequence_ids[SEQ_ID]]
clean_keypoints = fill_missing_keypoints(sequence.keypoints)
animation_obj = animate_pose_sequence(
    clean_keypoints,
    sequence_id=sequence.sequence_id,
    start_frame=0,
    stop_frame=240,
    step=6,
    interval_ms=80,
)
save_animation(animation_obj, repo_root / "outputs/visualizations/mabe_sequence_sample.mp4", fps=10)
```

## Compare a Future Trajectory Prediction

This cell uses a persistence baseline as a placeholder. Replace `predicted_future` with model output after converting Gaussian predictions back to pixel-space keypoints shaped `[future, 3, 12, 2]`.

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
SEQ_ID = 2
from pathlib import Path
import sys

import numpy as np

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src/data").exists())
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from data import MabeDataset, MabeWindowDataset, WindowSpec
from data.visualization import animate_prediction_comparison

dataset = MabeDataset.from_file(repo_root / "data/mabe/raw/mouse_triplet_train.npy")
sequence = dataset.sequences[dataset.sequence_ids[SEQ_ID]]
windows = MabeWindowDataset(
    [sequence],
    spec=WindowSpec(length=20, observation_length=8, prediction_length=12, stride=20),
    max_windows=1,
)
window = windows.first()
observed = window.observed_keypoints
future = window.future_keypoints
predicted_future = np.repeat(observed[-1:,...], repeats=future.shape[0], axis=0)

comparison_animation = animate_prediction_comparison(
    window.keypoints,
    predicted_future,
    observation_length=8,
    sequence_id=window.sequence_id,
    step=1,
    interval_ms=120,
)

comparison_animation
```

## Save Prediction Comparison

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
SEQ_ID = 2
from pathlib import Path
import sys

import numpy as np

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src/data").exists())
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from data import MabeDataset, MabeWindowDataset, WindowSpec
from data.visualization import animate_prediction_comparison, save_animation

dataset = MabeDataset.from_file(repo_root / "data/mabe/raw/mouse_triplet_train.npy")
sequence = dataset.sequences[dataset.sequence_ids[SEQ_ID]]
windows = MabeWindowDataset(
    [sequence],
    spec=WindowSpec(length=20, observation_length=8, prediction_length=12, stride=20),
    max_windows=1,
)
window = windows.first()
predicted_future = np.repeat(
    window.observed_keypoints[-1:, ...],
    repeats=window.future_keypoints.shape[0],
    axis=0,
)
comparison_animation = animate_prediction_comparison(
    window.keypoints,
    predicted_future,
    observation_length=8,
    sequence_id=window.sequence_id,
    step=1,
    interval_ms=120,
)
save_animation(comparison_animation, repo_root / "outputs/visualizations/persistence_baseline.mp4", fps=8)
```

## Interpretation Notes

- Solid skeletons show observed or ground-truth keypoints.
- Dashed skeletons and `x` markers show predicted future keypoints.
- Always inverse-transform normalized predictions before using this notebook.
- Use short clips first; rendering all 1800 frames is slow and rarely useful for debugging.
